  "section_notes": "S1 is strict: all incidents reported within 24h, full report in 10 days, customer notice in 72h, and reporting cannot wait for confirmation. S2 sets a 5% failure-rate threshold but does not automatically stop sales above it, leaving regulator discretion; per-model results go to purchasers and regulators but not the public. S3 delays new-unit shut-off by 3 years and allows a 6-year retrofit with a feasibility escape. S4 requires built-in suppression at 36 months with a validated equivalent option. S5 mandates recall above 8/100k with 72h customer notice."
